  "body": [
    "Powel’s Place is a business incubator for community-oriented ventures, combining education with subsidy. Classrooms and an auditorium occupy the renovated Samuel Powel Elementary School, while the incubator is distributed across the rest of the site, giving each business its own amenities and opening a range of outdoor spaces between them.",
    "The architectural language is simple and industrial, leaving the activity in the complex to carry the character.",
    "Environmental performance is a principal aim alongside the economic and educational ones. Solar panels, green roofs and efficient construction reduce the building's impact, and the site works as a grey-water and stormwater filtration system, cleaning runoff before it returns to the water table."
  ],
